# Build and Publish

## Build Outputs

- Bundler: tsup (CJS + ESM + DTS + sourcemaps) — see
  [tsup.config.ts](mdc:tsup.config.ts) and [tsup.config.v2.ts](mdc:tsup.config.v2.ts)
- Output dir: [dist/](mdc:dist/)
- Package exports configured in [package.json](mdc:package.json)
- Main build stems: `index` (V3 / AI SDK 6), `index-v2` (V2 / AI SDK 5,
  also AI SDK 6 compatibility), and `index-v4` (V4 / AI SDK 7), each with
  `.js`, `.cjs`, `.d.ts`, `.d.cts`, and JavaScript sourcemaps.
  The root and `/v3` share `index.*`: four entrypoints, three artifact families.

## Commands

### Build Commands

- Build the main package (V3 root, `/v2`, `/v3`, and `/v4`): `npm run build`
- Watch the main package build: `npm run build:watch`
- Build the standalone V2 package: `npm run build:v2`
- Watch the standalone V2 build: `npm run build:v2:watch`
- Prepare standalone V2 for npm publish: `npm run prepare:v2`
- Check all main-package entrypoints: `npm run check-build`
- Check one facade explicitly: `npm run check-build:v2` or `npm run check-build:v4`

### Quality Checks

- Type-check: `npm run type-check`
- Lint: `npm run lint`
- Lint-fix: `npm run lint-fix`
- Prettier-check: `npm run prettier-check`
- Prettier-fix: `npm run prettier-fix`
- Canonical Node tests: `npm run test:node` (`npm test` is an alias)
- Edge source tests: `npm run test:edge`
- Lockfile release age: `npm run check-lockfile-release-age` fetches canonical raw
  packuments and compares against
  `3f869c5f5371b35e53ef38bae2173541ab6c209a:package-lock.json`. Only registry
  artifacts absent from that lockfile are age-validated. `-- --all` validates
  every artifact; `-- --base <full-git-sha>` selects another comparison lockfile.
  The trusted workflow accepts raw head/base lockfile data via
  `--head-lockfile <path> --base-lockfile <path>` (all modes need registry access,
  fail closed, run without installed dependencies, limit each decoded packument to
  64 MiB and each UTF-8 lockfile to 2 MiB, and cap deduplicated selected artifacts
  at 1,024)
- Dependency advisory policy: `npm run check-dependency-audit` forces production,
  development, optional, and peer npm scopes. For exact audited instances it validates
  every edge up to the direct root anchor plus every edge identity entering that
  anchor; coherent shared references above it are not recursively traversed. npm 11
  `fixAvailable` must be its exact boolean/object union, and literal `true` rejects an
  exception (requires registry access)

### Versioned Entrypoints and Packages

This repository publishes two npm packages from the same codebase:

- `@jerome-benoit/sap-ai-provider` — V3 root plus `/v2`, `/v3`, and `/v4` subpaths
- `@jerome-benoit/sap-ai-provider-v2` — standalone V2 facade

`prepublishOnly` runs the appropriate build and verification before publish:

- Main package: `build && check-build`
- Standalone V2 (when `AI_SDK_VERSION=v2`):
  `build:v2 && check-build:v2 && prepare:v2`, followed by
  `tsx scripts/check-package-exports.ts` on the prepared package.

See [package.json](mdc:package.json) for the full script.

Both build configurations clean `dist/` first: `build:v2` replaces the main
package artifacts with V2-only outputs. `prepare:v2` renames `index-v2.*` to
`index.*`, updates JavaScript source-map references and any matching map `file`
metadata without changing mapped sources, rewrites the package name and AI peer
range to AI SDK 5/6, removes
`/v2`, `/v3`, and `/v4` exports from the manifest, and updates the lockfile.
Run publish preparation only in a disposable publishing checkout.

Before `npm ci`, run `npm run check-lockfile-release-age` as a local
non-authoritative candidate gate; it needs the public registry, runs without
`node_modules`, and fails closed if metadata is unavailable or incomplete. Dependency installation runs `prepare` (`lefthook install`), not a build.
Use `npm run build` explicitly to create distribution artifacts. npm
`min-release-age` applies while resolving, not when `npm ci` consumes the lockfile.
Policy is 3 days on `https://registry.npmjs.org/`. The checker uses top-level
packument `time[version]` and the matching version manifest fingerprint, limits
each decoded packument to 64 MiB, and uses eight metadata requests at a time, a
10-second fetch-and-body timeout, and fail-fast aborts. PR and autofix workflows
run non-authoritative candidate gates. The dedicated
`pull_request_target` workflow runs only trusted default-branch code, resolves exact
head/base commits through the GitHub API, and downloads only raw lockfiles as data.
It never imports, checks out, or executes the head and publishes status context
`dependency-security/trusted-lockfile-release-age` on the exact PR head; its
`push` job covers `main` with a 30-minute job timeout. Releases require that
exact-SHA trusted push run to report literal `main`, then re-run the checker. A
branch ruleset must require the exact status context and restrict its source. Since a shared GitHub Actions App identity cannot uniquely bind
that context to this workflow, an organization required workflow/Actions event policy
or dedicated external App must prevent homonymous/untrusted status writers. External
policy must protect the trusted/release workflows and policy files; no external policy
is claimed active.

## Node Engine

- Requires Node >= 22.12 (see `engines` in [package.json](mdc:package.json)).

## Verification

- Verify all main-package artifacts exist and ESM/CommonJS runtime and declaration
  routing resolves correctly: `npm run check-build`.
- Verify one facade build explicitly with `npm run check-build:v2` or
  `npm run check-build:v4`.
- `test:edge` exercises provider source behavior, not published-bundle
  portability. The ESM banner and SAP SDK dependencies use Node built-ins;
  do not infer pure Edge deployment support from that test suite.
